      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      
      <h3>What is a great 4-5 day itinerary for first time visit to Morocco?</h3>
      <p>If you only have 4-5 days, focus solely on Marrakech and the immediate surroundings. You can spend 2 days in the city and take our <strong>3-Day Premium Explorer</strong> to visit the Agafay Desert, Ourika Valley, and the Essaouira coast without wasting time on long bus rides.</p>

      <h3>Is 10 days in Morocco enough time?</h3>
      <p>Yes, 10 days is the "sweet spot" for a Moroccan vacation. It gives you enough time to comfortably visit the imperial cities (Marrakech and Fes), cross the High Atlas Mountains, and spend a night in the deep Sahara Desert without feeling utterly exhausted.</p>

